# Spark DS — React Components

## Before building custom UI

1. If implementing from Figma, run `get_design_context` and `search_design_system` (see `spark-ds-figma-mcp.mdc`).
2. Check `index.html` nav for documented components.
3. Read the component page for variants, props, anatomy, and usage guidelines.
4. Reuse or extend the shared Spark component. Do not recreate styled one-offs.

## Component standards

- Functional components with typed props.
- Use `forwardRef` on interactive primitives (Button, Input, Link).
- Native semantics: `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation (`href`), not `<div onClick>`.
- Compose classes with `clsx` / `cn`. Map props to documented class names.

## Button (documented in `button.html`)

Props align with Spark docs:

| Prop | Values |
|------|--------|
| `type` | `primary`, `secondary`, `tertiary`, `ghost`, `link`, `text` |
| `size` | `tiny`, `small`, `medium`, `large` |
| `danger` | boolean |
| `disabled` | boolean |
| `icon` | `ReactNode` (leading in DOM) |
| `iconEnd` | trailing icon visually |
| `iconOnly` | square icon button; requires `ariaLabel` |
| `href` | renders as anchor when set |

CSS classes: `spark-btn`, `spark-btn-{type}`, `spark-btn-{size}`, `spark-btn-icon-only`, `spark-btn-icon-end`, `spark-btn-disabled`, `spark-btn-danger`.

Styles must use tokens from `button.html` and `--semantic-button-*` in `tokens.css`.

## Modal (documented in `modal.html`)

Composes Modal `Type=Slot` (Figma) with Search-input. Use for focused flows with filterable slot content.

| Prop | Values |
|------|--------|
| `open` | boolean |
| `onClose` | `() => void` |
| `title` | string (required) |
| `subtitle` | string (optional) |
| `searchPlaceholder` | string (default `"Search"`) |
| `onSearchChange` | `(value: string) => void` (optional) |
| `primaryAction` | `{ label, onClick, disabled? }` |
| `secondaryAction` | `{ label, onClick, disabled? }` |
| `danger` | boolean (primary action uses danger button tokens) |
| `children` | `ReactNode` (slot body) |
| `closeOnOverlayClick` | boolean (default `true`) |

CSS classes:

- Root: `spark-modal` with `data-open` when visible
- Overlay: `spark-modal-overlay`
- Panel: `spark-modal-panel` with `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `aria-labelledby`
- Regions: `spark-modal-header`, `spark-modal-header-text`, `spark-modal-title`, `spark-modal-subtitle`, `spark-modal-search`, `spark-modal-body`, `spark-modal-footer`
- Search: `spark-search-input-wrap`, `spark-search-input`, `spark-search-input-icon`
- Close: `spark-btn spark-btn-ghost spark-btn-icon-only spark-btn-small` with `aria-label="Close"`

Footer buttons reuse `spark-btn-secondary` and `spark-btn-primary` (see Button). Tokens: `--semantic-modal-*`, `--semantic-search-input-*` in `tokens.css`.

Accessibility: trap focus while open, restore focus to trigger on close, `Escape` calls `onClose`, label the search field.

## Hierarchy

- One **Primary** button per view.
- Pair Primary with Secondary for main actions.
- Use **Danger** only for destructive actions.
- Prefer **Ghost** / **Text** in dense or inline contexts.

## Undocumented UI

If no Spark component exists, build with semantic tokens and match Button structure (focus ring, disabled states, sizes). Flag the gap; do not ship ad hoc patterns as permanent API.
